{"kind":"assert","text":"For Hugh: keep the review's human-facing lead stable when its coverage grows. The small improvement I recommend is to distinguish the artifact that explains the change from the reporting artifact that binds its implementation commitment. Show both clearly, while continuing to validate the complete exact-head artifact set. Adding a directory or generated-file companion should not replace the explanation readers see first.\n\nThe #21944 repair gives a concrete example. Review request #22196 named fold.go artifact 25ab386a first and added directory artifact 91f66c9f solely to complete succession coverage. Approval #22211 explained that it had to name the directory first because it was now the commitment's reporting artifact. The source head was unchanged. The repair is approved and landed; this note does not question that approval or reopen the task.\n\nThe coupling is explicit in the current source: [latestCompletion](internal/workroom/fold.go@359b211cfe94e758db592d6e4e78c2f85c6c9c30:3837) selects the newest eligible artifact before approval; [reportIndex](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@359b211cfe94e758db592d6e4e78c2f85c6c9c30:190) indexes only the commitment's selected report; and [resolveAssigned](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@359b211cfe94e758db592d6e4e78c2f85c6c9c30:318) requires that report to be primary. Thus filing order has a visible meaning that the author may not intend.\n\nKeep the remediation small. First separate the explanation shown to readers from the authoritative report used by review and merge checks, using existing artifact identities wherever possible. Then show one concise summary, its exact head and a count/list of all examined paths, with clickable file previews; label the authority anchor separately when it differs. Verify this with the actual 25-artifact repair packet, a one-file change and a stacked delivery: adding a companion must preserve the chosen explanation, while omissions, a different head, a foreign commitment or an unapproved underlying change still refuse.\n\nThis complements #21241's complete-change review recommendation: complete coverage and a stable explanation are both needed. It adds no approval stage and proposes no relaxation of lifecycle or merge authority. Existing commands must continue following their current primary rule until a reviewed change says otherwise. Evidence is the durable request and verdict plus source inspection, not a measured time saving or a new runtime reproduction. If adopted, the existing instructions and UI review work should share this example rather than create competing workflow rules.","body":{"head":"359b211cfe94e758db592d6e4e78c2f85c6c9c30","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0c874a64c0766504cda6d3da4733f1ca378b235b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7235fbca9f3dba128974089caa7afcdd3aafbefb stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0739dc3d9833620e90976f7858fbc66a9a781d8d and 62 more"}}